new file mode 100644
index 0000000..461bdd0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/rtc/TOV.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# WebRTC libraries, vendored
+
+`std/rtc` (WebRTC peer connections, data channels and RTP audio) runs on libdatachannel and the libraries it
+is built from. The files are the upstream ones, byte for byte, from these releases and commits; tests, examples,
+documentation, build scripts and programs are left out, and so are the parts the build does not compile.
+
+| Directory | Library | Version | Licence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `datachannel/` | [libdatachannel](https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libdatachannel) | v0.24.6 (`55f93686c01528224f448c19128836e7df245f72` is its commit) | MPL-2.0 (`datachannel/LICENSE`) |
+| `juice/` | [libjuice](https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libjuice) (ICE, STUN, TURN) | `b89c792e3612faf2f12cf35bcc56857313a06be3`, as pinned by libdatachannel v0.24.6 | MPL-2.0 (`juice/LICENSE`) |
+| `usrsctp/` | [usrsctp](https://github.com/sctplab/usrsctp) (SCTP, for data channels) | `fec583d54493f879d2ae44a743423bf8a04371ab`, as pinned | BSD (`usrsctp/LICENSE.md`) |
+| `srtp/` | [libsrtp](https://github.com/cisco/libsrtp) 2.8.0 | `24b3bf8f19b6f5ab4cd2bcceb4f4064efca86fd5`, as pinned | BSD (`srtp/LICENSE`) |
+| `plog/` | [plog](https://github.com/SergiusTheBest/plog) (headers) | `94899e0b926ac1b0f4750bfbd495167b4a6ae9ef`, as pinned | MIT (`plog/LICENSE`) |
+
+Files:
+- libdatachannel: `include/` and `src/` whole (its `deps/`, `examples/`, `test/`, `pages/` and `cmake/` are not here).
+- libjuice: `include/juice/juice.h` and `src/`.
+- usrsctp: `usrsctplib/` (the library; not its programs, fuzzers or documentation).
+- libsrtp: `include/srtp.h`, `srtp_priv.h`, `stream_list_priv.h`, `srtp/srtp.c`, `crypto/include/`, and the OpenSSL
+  backend's sources (`crypto/cipher/{cipher,cipher_test_cases,null_cipher,aes_icm_ossl,aes_gcm_ossl}.c`,
+  `crypto/hash/{auth,auth_test_cases,null_auth,hmac_ossl}.c`, `crypto/kernel/`, `crypto/math/`, `crypto/replay/`).
+  `config.h` is the one file of ours: what libsrtp's CMake writes for the OpenSSL backend, with the platform
+  choices made by the compiler's own macros.
+- plog: `include/`.
+
+How the build uses them (`crates/tov/src/build/rtc.rs`): every `.c` and `.cpp` file in `datachannel/src`,
+`juice/src`, `srtp/` and `usrsctp/usrsctplib` is compiled once per compiler into an archive with `runtime/rtc.c`,
+with the flags of the CMake builds of those libraries and the vendored BoringSSL's headers (the crypto library
+libdatachannel and libsrtp call). libdatachannel is C++17 with exceptions and RTTI, unlike BoringSSL's flags;
+its WebSocket support is compiled out (`RTC_ENABLE_WEBSOCKET=0`), its media support is on, and the usrsctp
+debugging output is off. Only programs that import `std/rtc` link the archive.
+
+To update: take the new libdatachannel release, its submodule commits and the same file lists, and rebuild
+(`make tov`, then `make tov-test`: `tov-patches/tests/rtc.tov` runs two peers against each other).
